# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: cador-intersectwith-missing — the ActiveX entity method IntersectWith did not exist on cador
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: cad-runtime
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-cador-intersectwith
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Symptom

Downstream SCHMS CI, under clautolisp's cador host:

: VLA-Object AutoCAD.Entity has no method named INTERSECTWITH

Both call forms failed:

: (vla-IntersectWith obj1 obj2 acExtendNone)
: (vlax-invoke obj1 'IntersectWith obj2 acExtendNone)

=vla-intersectwith= is in the SCHMS call inventory
(=issues/open/schms-call-inventory.md=, 2 calls).

* Cause

cador's entity-backed COM objects carry no method table: their methods are
answered by =%entity-fallback-method= (=clautolisp/cador/source/vlax-api.lisp=),
which knew only Delete / Erase / Update / Move / Rotate / Copy /
GetBoundingBox (and GetAttributes on an INSERT). Anything else fell through to
=:unknown-com-method=. The =acExtend*= constants were already bound (the
measured ActiveX enumeration table, 0..3).

* Vendor contract (Autodesk ActiveX reference, IntersectWith method)

: RetVal = object.IntersectWith(IntersectObject, ExtendOption)

- IntersectObject: the entity to intersect with.
- ExtendOption (AcExtendOption): =acExtendNone= 0 (neither extended),
  =acExtendThisEntity= 1 (the base), =acExtendOtherEntity= 2 (the argument),
  =acExtendBoth= 3.
- RetVal: VARIANT (array of doubles), the points flattened X1 Y1 Z1 X2 Y2 Z2
  ...; EMPTY when there is no intersection.

* Resolution (clautolisp 2.3.10 / alfe 2.3.10, branch fix-cador-intersectwith)

- =clautolisp/cador/source/intersect.lisp= (new): each entity is decomposed
  into curves on an underlying LINE / CIRCLE / ELLIPSE with a parameter range;
  the underlying shapes are intersected (line-line, line-circle,
  circle-circle, line-ellipse exactly; ellipse against circle / ellipse
  numerically: 2048 samples, bisection on sign changes, golden section on
  near-zero minima for tangencies), and each point is kept when it lies in
  both ranges.
  Supported: LINE, RAY, XLINE, CIRCLE, ARC, ELLIPSE (full or partial),
  LWPOLYLINE and 2D POLYLINE (bulged spans as true arcs, the OCS for
  extrusion +Z / -Z), 3D POLYLINE (3D segments). SPLINE, meshes, polyface
  meshes, text, inserts, points etc. and any entity whose extrusion is not
  +Z / -Z signal =:unsupported-com-geometry= ("IntersectWith: AcDbSpline is
  not a curve IntersectWith handles; clautolisp does not support it.").
- =%entity-fallback-method= answers "IntersectWith" (and
  =vlax-method-applicable-p= says so); the result goes through the
  =*com-point-wrap-hook*=, i.e. the same VARIANT(SAFEARRAY of doubles) as a
  point property; an empty intersection is an EMPTY safearray (bounds 0 .. -1),
  not nil, and =vlax-invoke= converts it to the flat list or nil.
- Option validation: an ExtendOption other than 0..3, a non-entity argument,
  or a third argument signal =:invalid-com-argument=.
- Tests: =clautolisp/cador/tests/intersect-tests.lisp= (6 tests, 200 checks:
  every pair under the 4 options),
  =clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/tests/intersectwith-tests.lisp=
  (7 tests, 20 checks: both call forms, VARIANT / SAFEARRAY shape, empty
  result, constants, applicability, catchable unsupported error).
- Docs: user manual, the ActiveX section (IntersectWith bullet);
  RELEASE_NOTES.org. The spec has no page for ActiveX methods, so no
  =*** clautolisp= section.
- Probe: =autolisp-front-end/tests/scenarios/entities/intersectwith-probe.lsp=,
  driven by =scripts/run-intersectwith-probe.{sh,ps1}=; CI jobs (family
  =intersectwith= in =scripts/ci-detect-probe-changes.py=):
  =intersectwith:probe:bricscad:macos=, =intersectwith:probe:bricscad:windows=,
  =intersectwith:probe:autocad:windows= (GUI, COM automation),
  =intersectwith:probe:accoreconsole:windows= (in =.gitlab/native.yml=) and
  =intersectwith:probe:clautolisp:linux= (parent, manual). Output lines
  =IWPROBE <pair>.<option>.<field>=<value>=, artefact =dist/intersectwith/=.

* TO MEASURE (as filed; answered below, 2026-10-08)

All in the source as SPEC-UNCERTAIN (intersect.lisp header).

1. *Point order.* cador sorts along the BASE object: a line from its start,
   a circle counter-clockwise from angle 0, an arc from its start angle, an
   ellipse from parameter 41, a polyline span by span (a point on the
   backward extension of its first span sorts first). Probe pairs
   LINE-CIRCLE-TWO vs LINE-CIRCLE-TWO-REVERSED vs CIRCLE-LINE-TWO,
   CIRCLE-LINE-VERTICAL, CIRCLE-CIRCLE-TWO(-SWAPPED), PLINE-CIRCLE.
2. *Polyline extension rule.* An open polyline extends only its first span
   backwards and its last span forwards (an arc span to its full circle); a
   closed one does not extend. PLINE-LINE-EXTENDED, LINE-PLINE-EXTENDED,
   PLINECLOSED-LINE-EXTENDED, POLYLINE2D-LINE-EXTENDED.
3. *Ray extension.* acExtendThisEntity on a RAY makes it the infinite line
   (not in the probe yet: the RAY / XLINE cases are unit tests only).
4. *Tangency* = one point (LINE-CIRCLE-TANGENT, CIRCLE-CIRCLE-TANGENT).
5. *Overlaps* = no point: collinear overlapping lines (LINE-LINE-COLLINEAR),
   concentric / coincident circles (CIRCLE-CIRCLE-CONCENTRIC). The vendor
   may return the overlap's end points.
6. *Duplicates*: a crossing at a polyline vertex is reported once
   (PLINE-LINE-VERTICES).
7. *Z*: two segments crossing in plan at different heights do not meet
   (LINE-LINE-SKEWZ); the vendor may project.
8. *Empty result*: =vlax-safearray->list= of the empty array returns nil in
   clautolisp; the vendor may signal (the TOLIST field is written for every
   call, empty or not). The bounds (0 .. -1) are also to confirm.
9. *vlax-variant-type* of the result: the vendor returns 8197 (8192 + 5,
   array of doubles); clautolisp returns the symbol ARRAY -- a separate,
   pre-existing defect, =vlax-variant-type-returns-a-symbol.issue=.
10. Whether AcCoreConsole answers IntersectWith at all (it has no application
    object): =intersectwith:probe:accoreconsole:windows=.

When the results are in: replace the SPEC-UNCERTAIN marker with Vendor:
citations, adjust the order / extension / overlap choices to the measured
behaviour (with dialect-divergence classification if AutoCAD and BricsCAD
differ), and close.

* Measurements (2026-10-08, MR !462, branch head e22c528e)

intersectwith-probe.lsp on four targets (artefacts dist/intersectwith/):

| job         | target                                   | IWPROBE lines |
|-------------+------------------------------------------+---------------|
| 17029587295 | intersectwith:probe:autocad:windows (AutoCAD 2022, 24.1s, GUI via COM) | 1159 + DONE |
| 17029587293 | intersectwith:probe:bricscad:macos (BricsCAD V26)    | 1158 + DONE |
| 17029587294 | intersectwith:probe:bricscad:windows (BricsCAD V25)  | 1159 + DONE |
| 17029587296 | intersectwith:probe:accoreconsole:windows (AutoCAD 2022 AcCoreConsole) | 206 + DONE |

Coordinates: the probe builds its geometry from short literals (and pi
computed on the CAD side), so alfe's real rounding
(alfe-cad-transport-rounds-reals) does not reach them; all values are
compared to 1e-3 and agree. The two BricsCAD builds agree on every line.
The Windows reports end with a false "IWPROBE-INCOMPLETE": the .ps1
re-read its own mixed UTF-8 / UTF-16 report (fixed for this probe;
probe-ps1-done-check-misreads-utf16-report.issue for the siblings).

Clautolisp's column: the same probe on the built clautolisp-sbcl --host
mock, under --dialect autocad and --dialect bricscad.

1. *Point order* -- DIVERGENT, and not a sort along the base object on
   either vendor (what 2f546bf1 did). The point SETS agree everywhere; the order is each pair's solver order:
   - line x CIRCLE: the point farther from the line's start first, on both,
     whichever is the base: LINE-CIRCLE-TWO.0.INVOKE=(5 0 0 -5 0 0),
     LINE-CIRCLE-TWO-REVERSED.0.INVOKE=(-5 0 0 5 0 0),
     CIRCLE-LINE-TWO = (5 0 0 -5 0 0), CIRCLE-LINE-VERTICAL = (0 5 0 0 -5 0);
   - line x ARC: descending offset from the arc's start (the start counting
     as a whole turn), on both: LINE-ARC-TWO.0.INVOKE=(-4 3 0 4 3 0),
     LINE-ARC-EXTARC.2.INVOKE=(4 -3 0 -4 -3 0), LINE-ARC-ENDS = (5 0 0 -5 0 0);
   - circle/arc x circle/arc: mid + h perp first (perp: left of base centre
     -> other centre) on both; but AutoCAD answers options 2 and 3 as the
     ARGUMENT's IntersectWith: CIRCLE-CIRCLE-TWO.2.INVOKE AutoCAD
     (3 -4 0 3 4 0), BricsCAD (3 4 0 3 -4 0); ARC-ARC-ONE.3 likewise;
   - polylines span by span; a bulge span: AutoCAD takes it as the
     counter-clockwise arc it is stored as (and as the SECOND of a span x
     circle pair), BricsCAD in its travel direction (as the first):
     PLINE-LINE-ARCSPAN.0.INVOKE AutoCAD (-2.236068 5 0 2.236068 5 0),
     BricsCAD (2.236068 5 0 -2.236068 5 0); PLINE-CIRCLE.1.INVOKE AutoCAD
     (-3 -4 0 -2.763854 4.166667 0 2.763854 4.166667 0 3 -4 0), BricsCAD
     (-3 -4 0 2.763854 4.166667 0 -2.763854 4.166667 0 3 -4 0);
   - ellipse x circle: AutoCAD along the ellipse's parameter
     (3.464102 3.605551 0 -3.464102 3.605551 0 ...), BricsCAD by ascending X
     then descending Y (-3.464102 3.605551 0 -3.464102 -3.605551 0
     3.464102 3.605551 0 3.464102 -3.605551 0); line x ellipse: farther first
     on both (ELLIPSE-LINE = (8 0 0 -8 0 0)).
2. *Polyline extension* -- as implemented, on both: first span backwards,
   last forwards (PLINE-LINE-EXTENDED.1.INVOKE=(-3 -5 0 3 -5 0), and .2 nil);
   a closed polyline does not extend (PLINECLOSED-LINE-EXTENDED.* nil);
   POLYLINE2D-LINE-EXTENDED identical.
3. *Ray extension* -- not in the probe; unchanged (SPEC-UNCERTAIN,
   deferred-spec-research.issue).
4. *Tangency* -- one point on both (LINE-CIRCLE-TANGENT = (0 5 0),
   CIRCLE-CIRCLE-TANGENT = (5 0 0)).
5. *Overlaps* -- no point on both (LINE-LINE-COLLINEAR.*, CIRCLE-CIRCLE-
   CONCENTRIC.* nil).
6. *Vertex crossing* -- once on both (PLINE-LINE-VERTICES = (-3 3 0 3 3 0)).
7. *Z* -- crossing in plan at different Z: no point on both
   (LINE-LINE-SKEWZ.* nil).
8. *Empty result* -- bounds 0 .. -1 on both (LINE-LINE-PARALLEL.0.UBOUND=-1);
   vlax-safearray->list of it is an ERROR on both: AutoCAD "Le serveur
   ActiveX a renvoye une erreur: Index non valide" (ActiveX Server returned
   an error: Invalid index), BricsCAD "bad argument type <#<safearray...>> ;
   expected SAFEARRAY at [vlax-safearray->list]". vlax-invoke gives nil.
9. *vlax-variant-type* -- 8197 for a non-empty result on both; for the EMPTY
   one AutoCAD 8197, BricsCAD 8204 (an array of VARIANTs).
10. *AcCoreConsole* -- has no COM entity objects at all:
    (vlax-ename->vla-object e) fails with "type d'argument incorrect:
    VLA-OBJECT nil" for every entity, so IntersectWith cannot be called
    (every pair NO-BASE-OBJECT). Nothing to reproduce: clautolisp has no
    AcCoreConsole dialect.

Also observed: AutoCAD prints (type v) of a VARIANT / SAFEARRAY as
"variant" / "safearray" through vl-princ-to-string (BricsCAD "VARIANT");
type-symbols-print-lowercase-on-autocad.issue.

* Resolution of the measurements (clautolisp 2.3.10 / alfe 2.3.10, same branch)

- intersect.lisp reproduces each vendor's order (rules above), chosen by
  the dialect's PRODUCT: BricsCAD under a BricsCAD dialect, AutoCAD
  otherwise (strict, autocad, clautolisp, lax). The order is an
  UNRESOLVED divergence (the reference says nothing): every dialect but lax
  prints [intersectwith-order] when the two vendors' orders differ for the
  call.
- The empty result: an empty array of doubles (8197, AutoCAD, as the
  reference says) -- of VARIANTs (8204) under a BricsCAD dialect, which
  warns [intersectwith-empty], as strict does (resolved divergence,
  AutoCAD normative; %resolved-divergence-policy).
- vlax-safearray->list of an array with no element signals, with the
  product's message.
- vlax-variant-type returns the vlax-vb* code (8197 for the result), and
  vlax-safearray-type too; vlax-make-variant / vlax-variant-change-type /
  vlax-make-safearray accept integer type codes
  (vlax-variant-type-returns-a-symbol, closed with this).
- With the change, the probe's clautolisp column equals AutoCAD's under
  --dialect autocad and BricsCAD's (both builds) under --dialect bricscad
  on all 1157 lines, apart from the error messages' language and the
  lowercase type names above.
- Tests: cador intersect-tests 7 tests / 210 checks (AutoCAD order, and
  intersectwith-bricscad-order); builtins intersectwith-tests 9 tests / 50 checks with the variant / safearray tests
  (dialect order, empty shape per product, variant type codes).

Remaining, deferred (deferred-spec-research.issue, IntersectWith): orders in
cases the probe did not exercise -- a line starting beyond a circle's
centre, clockwise (-Z) ARC entities, rays / xlines, 3D polylines, ellipse
pairs beyond the one measured -- follow the same rules by extension.
